    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "walking out of the room feels like something you can just do in movies. in real life, everything is just tied together. work, family, just... existing. there's no exit door. it just feels like a constant, heavy weight that never goes away no matter how much i try to mask or adapt. i'm just so done with the effort of it all.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
